.TH PWD 1 "2026" "spicule" "spicule User Commands"
.SH NAME
pwd \- return working directory name
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pwd
.RB [ \-L | \-P ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pwd
writes an absolute pathname of the current working directory to
standard output, followed by a newline.
.PP
.B pwd
takes no operands; giving it any operand at all is an error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-L
Accepted. Has the same effect as no option at all (see
.B \-P
below).
.TP
.B \-P
Accepted. The pathname written contains no components that refer to
symbolic links, because it is obtained directly from the operating
system rather than from any shell-tracked notion of the current
directory; this is also what happens with no option, and with
.B \-L
, so all three cases behave identically.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The pathname of the current working directory was written
successfully.
.TP
.B 1
The current working directory could not be determined, or writing the
pathname to standard output failed.
.TP
.B 2
An operand, or an option other than
.B \-L
or
.BR \-P ,
was given.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR realpath (1)
